WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:05.550
Let's go next to our caller from the five
one nine area code.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.460
Who's calling today from five one nine?

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.610
And just as importantly, where are you calling
from?

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.219
David?

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:14.839
Yes.

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:16.450
OK.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.360
It's really from Owen Sound, Ontario, Canada.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:22.470
Got a question for you.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.470
Yes.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:28.380
Do you think that maybe Mr. Trump is just
fed up with the job and is deliberately trying

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.710
to sabotage his reelection?

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.260
I think he wants to go golfing, I think.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.260
Yeah.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.260
You're not ready for him.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.660
You're not the only person to ask about out
of office.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.129
He can raise all the hell he wants.

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:40.129
Yeah.

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:41.399
Not have to take any responsibility for it.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:42.399
Right.

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:43.399
Your views on that.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:44.399
Let's hear.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:45.940
A few people have asked me about this.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.109
Save a night.

00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:48.480
David, I can't hear you.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.940
My phone's acting up, so I'm just going to
hang up and watch for your response on the

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.940
show sometime.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.940
OK, ok.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:54.940
That sounds fine.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:01.769
Listen, I don't believe Trump is consciously
trying to sabotage or sabotage his own election.

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:04.949
I think Trump's ego won't let him do it.

00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:12.530
But I do believe that if Trump loses, he will
justify it by saying, hey, you know what?

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:13.790
It was rigged.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.640
And I have plenty of things to do.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.110
I'm still a rich guy.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.079
I'm still going to be able to go and, you
know, do do whatever it is that I want.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:25.280
So I don't think Trump is deliberately sabotaging
himself.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.659
I think from the beginning, Trump didn't really
want to be president.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:35.229
And were the Republican electorate not so
easily bamboozled, Bill?

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:39.649
If that's a word, Trump never would have become
their nominee and would never be president

00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:40.860
to this day.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:47.250
But, yeah, I think that if Trump is trying
to sabotage his election, he's doing it subconsciously,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.250
not consciously.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:53.130
And then he will, after the fact, certainly
say I'm better off doing doing other stuff

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:53.460
anyway.

